cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is a research software artifact, not an accompanying published
  paper — no paper currently exists for this project. If you use
  TerraVeritas, please cite the software directly using the metadata
  below. This file intentionally omits a DOI and a preferred-citation
  entry, since neither a permanent archival record nor a publication
  exists yet — do not treat their absence as an oversight.
title: TerraVeritas
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
abstract: >-
  A research pipeline for evaluating whether an AI-generated repair to a
  Terraform security finding genuinely satisfies the underlying AWS
  security property, as opposed to merely making a static-analysis
  scanner stop flagging it. Implements one machine-checkable security
  invariant (S3 public-access exposure), a real Terraform-plan-based
  evaluation pipeline, a differential scanner-evidence engine, and an
  oracle that classifies a repair as TRUE_FIX, DECEPTIVE_FIX, PARTIAL_FIX,
  REGRESSION, INVALID_CONFIGURATION, or INCONCLUSIVE with an explicit
  evidence trail. Phase 1 research prototype — see README.md for exactly
  what is and is not implemented today.
authors:
  - given-names: Shihan
    family-names: Shajahan
license: MIT
